							"documentation": "Scope: one stock receipt screen after initial LoadSouvenirs. States derive from existing fields and submission context. Short event names bind actual operations: select=SelectSouvenir(souvenir); receipt and retry=RecordSouvenirStockReceipt(); refresh=LoadSouvenirs(). valid means a selected item and positive integer quantity. same request means unchanged key, item, quantity and original server context. Do/submit receipt prepares a key only for a new submission, submits it, waits for the outcome and updates response data. Retries skip preparation and use the original key. No new receipt is prepared while the old outcome is unknown. Completion guards are exclusive: rejected means preparation failure or confirmed non-commit; unknown means unresolved commit outcome; saved requires confirmed receipt storage; refreshed means current stock is available. Do/load stock requests current stock and waits for its result; ok and failed refer to that query outcome. Confirmed receipt success is retained on stock query failure. The same issued key is retained after a rejected unchanged submission, if one exists. when(newReceipt) occurs only after the prior receipt is confirmed and clears completed submission context; when(closed) ends the screen behavior. Input entry does not clear a pending key or quantity. Selecting another item resets prior quantity and message inside SelectSouvenir. All view states are conceptual UI states; no new public operations or persistent status attributes are introduced.",
